---
import NerdBox from "@/components/caira/NerdBox.astro";
---

<div class="reveal">
  <div class="fig">
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 720 250"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Tenant resolution: WhatsApp phone_number_id resolves to a clinic_id, which scopes every downstream query"
    >
      <defs>
        <marker
          id="t-ar"
          markerWidth="9"
          markerHeight="9"
          refX="7"
          refY="4"
          orient="auto"
        >
          <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" style="fill:var(--cx-teal)"></path>
        </marker>
        <marker
          id="t-arR"
          markerWidth="9"
          markerHeight="9"
          refX="7"
          refY="4"
          orient="auto"
        >
          <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" style="fill:var(--cx-red)"></path>
        </marker>
        <style is:inline>
          .tb {
            fill: var(--cx-ink3);
            stroke: var(--cx-line2);
          }
          .tg {
            fill: var(--cx-teal-dim);
            stroke: var(--cx-teal);
            stroke-width: 1.4;
          }
          .tr {
            fill: var(--cx-red-dim);
            stroke: var(--cx-red);
            stroke-width: 1.2;
            stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
          }
          .tt2 {
            font-family: var(--cx-mono);
            font-size: 10px;
            fill: var(--cx-text);
          }
          .ts2 {
            font-family: var(--cx-mono);
            font-size: 8.5px;
            fill: var(--cx-muted);
          }
          .tl {
            stroke: var(--cx-teal);
            stroke-width: 1.5;
            fill: none;
            marker-end: url(#t-ar);
          }
          .tlr {
            stroke: var(--cx-red);
            stroke-width: 1.4;
            fill: none;
            marker-end: url(#t-arR);
          }
          .tlab {
            font-family: var(--cx-mono);
            font-size: 8px;
            fill: var(--cx-faint);
          }
        </style>
      </defs>

      <rect class="tb" x="10" y="20" width="164" height="56" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="tt2" x="22" y="41">inbound payload</text>
      <text class="ts2" x="22" y="56">metadata.phone_number_id</text>
      <text class="ts2" x="22" y="69">= 1084…41 ← physical</text>

      <rect class="tr" x="10" y="150" width="164" height="56" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="tt2" x="22" y="171" style="fill:var(--cx-red-soft)"
        >anything claiming</text
      >
      <text class="ts2" x="22" y="186" style="fill:var(--cx-red-soft)"
        >"clinic_id": "&lt;other&gt;"</text
      >
      <text class="ts2" x="22" y="199" style="fill:var(--cx-red-soft)"
        >in the body → IGNORED</text
      >

      <rect class="tg" x="228" y="70" width="200" height="72" rx="11"></rect>
      <text class="tt2" x="242" y="92" style="fill:var(--cx-teal)"
        >clinic resolver</text
      >
      <text class="ts2" x="242" y="108">one receiving number maps</text>
      <text class="ts2" x="242" y="121">to exactly one clinic</text>
      <text class="ts2" x="242" y="135" style="fill:var(--cx-amber)"
        >1 indexed lookup · no scan</text
      >

      <rect class="tb" x="482" y="18" width="228" height="48" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="tt2" x="494" y="38">clinic_id (server-derived)</text>
      <text class="ts2" x="494" y="54"
        >the only tenant identity that exists</text
      >

      <rect class="tb" x="482" y="80" width="228" height="52" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="tt2" x="494" y="100">tenant wrapper</text>
      <text class="ts2" x="494" y="116"
        >pins the clinic onto the transaction</text
      >
      <text class="ts2" x="494" y="128">→ transaction-scoped, never leaks</text>

      <rect class="tb" x="482" y="146" width="228" height="52" rx="9"></rect>
      <text class="tt2" x="494" y="166">RLS policy on every tenant table</text>
      <text class="ts2" x="494" y="182"
        >rows visible only to their own clinic</text
      >
      <text class="ts2" x="494" y="194">enforced by the database itself</text>

      <rect
        class="tb"
        x="228"
        y="176"
        width="200"
        height="46"
        rx="9"
        stroke-dasharray="3 3"></rect>
      <text class="tt2" x="240" y="196">unknown number</text>
      <text class="ts2" x="240" y="211">→ null → message dropped</text>

      <path class="tl flow-dash" d="M174,48 C200,48 204,88 226,96"></path>
      <path class="tlr flow-dash" d="M174,178 C196,178 200,150 210,124 L224,112"
      ></path>
      <path class="tl flow-dash" d="M428,92 C452,88 458,52 480,44"></path>
      <path class="tl flow-dash" d="M596,66 L596,78"></path>
      <path class="tl flow-dash" d="M596,132 L596,144"></path>
      <path class="tl flow-dash" d="M328,142 L328,174"></path>
      <text class="tlab" x="186" y="82">physical arrival</text>
      <text class="tlab" x="176" y="146">forged claim</text>
    </svg>
    <div class="figcap">
      Green solid: identity derived from the letterbox, trusted. Red dashed:
      whatever the visitor claims, ignored.
    </div>
  </div>

  <NerdBox title="the three backstops behind the letterbox">
    <p>
      Resolving the receiving number to a clinic is one indexed lookup against
      a unique index, no table scan. From there every tenant row in the
      database carries its own clinic id, and every repository call takes that
      clinic id explicitly. Row-level security is the designed backstop: a
      small wrapper pins the current clinic onto the database transaction, and
      policies on the rows themselves refuse to serve another clinic's data,
      in case a developer ever forgets a WHERE clause.
    </p>
  </NerdBox>
</div>
